{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/task\/cancel()"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/cancel()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling a task has three primary effects:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It flags the task as canceled."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It causes any active cancellation handlers on the task to run, once."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It cancels any child tasks and task groups of the task, including"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those created in the future. If those tasks have cancellation handlers,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they also are triggered."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Task cancellation is cooperative and idempotent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancelling a task does not automatically cause arbitrary functions on the task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to stop running or throw errors. A function ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"may"}]},{"type":"text","text":" choose to react"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to cancellation by ending its work early, and it is conventional to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signal that to callers by throwing "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". However,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"a function that doesn’t specifically check for cancellation will","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"run to completion normally, even if the task it is running on is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"canceled. However, that function might still end early if it calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other code that handles cancellation by throwing and that function doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handle the error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s safe to cancel a task from any task or thread. It’s safe for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiple tasks or threads to cancel the same task at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time. Cancelling a task that has already been canceled has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"additional effect."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancel"},{"type":"text","text":" may need to acquire locks and synchronously run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arbitrary cancellation-handler code associated with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"canceled task. To reduce the risk of deadlock, it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recommended that callers release any locks they might be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holding before they call cancel."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the task has already run past the last point where it could have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"performed a cancellation check, cancelling it may have no observable effects."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"See Also","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text"